{"id": "DemAkKPylxh", "title": "Video by devanshu.motion", "description": "Many of you asked why Maa Kali's tongue is out. There are two kathas: one in the granth, one in the parampara 🙏\n\nThis is the granth. In the Devi Mahatmya (Markandeya Purana, chapter 8), every drop of Raktabeej's blood that reached the earth raised a new asur. So Chandika told Kali: Chamunda, open your mouth wide. Kali took the blood into her mouth before a single drop touched the ground, chewed up the asurs born there, and Raktabeej fell to Chandika's weapons. Then the Matrikas danced, and the gods rejoiced.\n\nThe story of Mahadev lying in her path is not in this text. It comes from the tradition of Bengal and Odisha, the one you saw in Part 2. Told as Tholu Bommalata, Andhra's leather shadow puppets 🪔\n\nNavdurga, Day 7, Part 3: the granth version.\n\nSources: Devi Mahatmya, chapter 8 · Usha Menon & Richard Shweder, \"Kali's Tongue\" (1994)\n\nSend this to the friend who argued about it in the comments 👀\n\n#navratri #maakali #devimahatmya #chamunda #indianart", "channel": "devanshu.motion", "uploader_id": "25176808901", "uploader": "Devanshu Singhai", "timestamp": 1792236937, "like_count": 8920, "comment_count": 46, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1859526705480997a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 55.498, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQOC7zQDxXZLDZtB9MAOJiawWqUUjsOl0Lzrix14YHgEBAi58ORaKm3VeCmZbx88YGE2nn1I4moAtru3_mUr12CGVoB42hDERSyFD3c.mp4?_nc_cat=101&_nc_oc=AdrZQP7w7HimalBsNDnHmnWkz_M17y_TegI1qiMjFNux85hrPJLCRUk7yT24QH9D7feCFeCa606kijDffLXLmWYD&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr22-2.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=dFaZYu6ppnoQ7kNvwEcYYEh&%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=52FuTK5u-RQN_qORLZ6Qzg&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQRI322mL-YiLCT67a6ldsomOkdqfryoCjbM91ZA08-IbQ&oe=6AF41906", "manifest_